WEBVTT

00:00:55.473 --> 00:00:56.682
It is no surprise to me,

00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:59.226
that these Northmen

00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:59.226
have arrived in Wessex.

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:01.061
After I heard about their

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:01.061
raids into Northumbria,

00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:03.022
I realized it was only

00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:03.022
a matter of time,

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:05.065
before they came ashore here.

00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:11.990
When I lived at the court

00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:11.990
of the Emperor Charlemagne,

00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:14.742
of long and blessed memory,

00:01:16.452 --> 00:01:19.246
these Northmen had already

00:01:16.452 --> 00:01:19.246
emerged, from their lairs,

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:20.748
to attack parts of his empire.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.209
And I remember an incident,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.209
from this period very well.

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:26.838
I was with Charlemagne's party,

00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:29.590
at a harbor town,

00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:29.590
in southern Gaul.

00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:32.092
As we sat eating supper,

00:01:32.134 --> 00:01:35.179
a fleet of pirates

00:01:32.134 --> 00:01:35.179
attacked the harbor.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.641
There was some confusion

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.641
about their identity,

00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.644
but from the build

00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.644
of their ships, and their

00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.644
speed through the water,

00:01:41.686 --> 00:01:45.147
the Emperor recognized them

00:01:41.686 --> 00:01:45.147
at once as Northmen.

00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:49.027
After a lightning attack...

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:54.991
They made their escape.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:02:01.413
The Emperor's men

00:01:55.033 --> 00:02:01.413
took up the chase,

00:01:55.033 --> 00:02:01.413
but, they were soon out-sailed.

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:06.168
Charlemagne, rose

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:06.168
from the table, and stood

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:06.168
at the window, facing east.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.129
I remember it as clearly,

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.129
as if it were yesterday.

00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.843
For a long time he stood,

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:18.472
while the tears,

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:18.472
poured down his face.

00:02:20.307 --> 00:02:22.184
In the end, he said,

00:02:22.226 --> 00:02:25.270
Do you know why

00:02:22.226 --> 00:02:25.270
I weep so bitterly?

00:02:25.312 --> 00:02:26.856
It's not because I'm afraid,

00:02:26.898 --> 00:02:29.274
these ruffians

00:02:26.898 --> 00:02:29.274
will do me any harm.

00:02:29.316 --> 00:02:32.111
I am sick at heart

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.113
to think, that

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.113
even in my lifetime,

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:37.199
they have dared

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:37.199
to attack this coast.

00:02:37.241 --> 00:02:39.660
And I am horror-stricken,

00:02:39.702 --> 00:02:41.996
when I foresee,

00:02:39.702 --> 00:02:41.996
what evil they will do,

00:02:42.038 --> 00:02:44.331
to my descendants

00:02:42.038 --> 00:02:44.331
and their subjects.

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:51.171
And now, it is our turn,

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:51.171
to deal with these ruffians.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:53.632
These pagans.

00:02:56.844 --> 00:02:58.846
But deal with them we shall.

00:03:01.057 --> 00:03:02.182
And must.

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:06.729
Aethelwulf?

00:03:08.397 --> 00:03:09.774
Yes, Father.

00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:13.318
I put it in your hands,

00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:13.318
to work with our ealdormen,

00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:13.318
to raise an army.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.947
In the meantime,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.947
we shall send spies and others,

00:03:15.988 --> 00:03:20.367
to observe the size

00:03:15.988 --> 00:03:20.367
of the raiding party,

00:03:15.988 --> 00:03:20.367
and their intentions.

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:23.037
These Northmen

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:23.037
never like to venture

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:23.037
far from their ships,

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:26.707
and they prefer not to be

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:26.707
drawn into pitched battle.

00:03:26.749 --> 00:03:29.919
Let us not be afraid,

00:03:26.749 --> 00:03:29.919
but rather watchful.

00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:33.255
And ultimately, decisive.

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:36.425
As the Emperor was.

00:03:54.193 --> 00:03:56.487
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:09.125
What is that place?

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:10.835
It's a Christian church,

00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:13.171
a minster.

00:04:13.212 --> 00:04:15.089
A large one.

00:04:13.212 --> 00:04:15.089
It may be Winchester.

00:04:15.798 --> 00:04:17.175
Is it important?

00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:19.802
If it is Winchester,

00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:19.802
Saint Birinus is

00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:19.802
buried there.

00:04:19.844 --> 00:04:21.512
It's a place of

00:04:19.844 --> 00:04:21.512
great pilgrimage.

00:04:21.553 --> 00:04:23.514
And will there

00:04:21.553 --> 00:04:23.514
be treasure there?

00:04:24.974 --> 00:04:27.559
Yes. A lot

00:04:24.974 --> 00:04:27.559
of treasure.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:28.978
(CHUCKLES)

00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:44.284
(EAGLE SCREECHES)

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.756
SIGVARD: Lagertha!

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.765
Why must I follow

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.765
you up the fields?

00:05:07.558 --> 00:05:09.977
You're my wife.

00:05:10.019 --> 00:05:13.898
You should be at my side,

00:05:10.019 --> 00:05:13.898
especially when we

00:05:10.019 --> 00:05:13.898
have important guests.

00:05:13.939 --> 00:05:16.108
I will not stay to

00:05:13.939 --> 00:05:16.108
hear my son insulted.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.194
Your son should

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.194
know his place.

00:05:18.236 --> 00:05:19.778
He continues

00:05:18.236 --> 00:05:19.778
to be resentful.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.323
He refuses to

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.323
accept or acknowledge

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.323
my love for him.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.411
You don't

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.411
love my son.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.330
You don't love

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.330
anyone, Sigvard.

00:05:31.832 --> 00:05:33.084
You don't know how to.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:34.626
(GROANS)

00:05:41.884 --> 00:05:44.136
Forgive me, Lagertha.

00:05:41.884 --> 00:05:44.136
I'm an intemperate man.

00:05:52.978 --> 00:05:56.607
I find it difficult

00:05:52.978 --> 00:05:56.607
to control myself.

00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:59.277
But I have loved

00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:59.277
and desired you

00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:59.277
after my fashion,

00:06:00.485 --> 00:06:03.281
and if your son will

00:06:00.485 --> 00:06:03.281
only meet me halfway,

00:06:04.323 --> 00:06:06.867
I will make sure he

00:06:04.323 --> 00:06:06.867
has a good future.

00:06:38.107 --> 00:06:40.734
(SHEEP BLEATING)

00:06:44.029 --> 00:06:47.074
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

00:06:51.703 --> 00:06:53.122
(SHUDDERING)

00:06:55.874 --> 00:06:57.626
(BELL TOLLING)

00:06:57.668 --> 00:06:58.794
MAN 1: The alarm!

00:06:58.836 --> 00:07:01.213
(CLAMORING)

00:07:02.006 --> 00:07:03.382
MAN 2: Inside, now!

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.135
(BELL CONTINUES TOLLING)

00:07:07.178 --> 00:07:10.097
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

00:07:16.687 --> 00:07:17.604
(GROANS)

00:07:20.232 --> 00:07:22.442
(CROWD SCREAMING)

00:07:25.279 --> 00:07:26.446
Ready?

00:07:26.989 --> 00:07:28.407
Weapons!

00:07:36.123 --> 00:07:39.335
(BELL CONTINUES TOLLING)

00:07:45.507 --> 00:07:47.843
(ANIMALS BLEATING)

00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:56.227
(SHOUTING)

00:07:56.935 --> 00:07:57.978
(SHOUTS)

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:02.983
(GRUNTS)

00:08:07.612 --> 00:08:08.488
(MAN SCREAMS)

00:08:10.157 --> 00:08:11.200
(SHOUTS)

00:08:13.577 --> 00:08:14.494
(SHOUTS)

00:08:19.417 --> 00:08:20.459
(SCREAMS)

00:08:23.545 --> 00:08:24.504
(SCREAMS)

00:08:25.464 --> 00:08:27.216
(GRUNTING)

00:08:40.104 --> 00:08:41.105
(PANTING)

00:08:41.897 --> 00:08:42.940
(GRUNTS)

00:08:43.732 --> 00:08:45.109
(SCREAMING)

00:08:45.859 --> 00:08:47.611
(SCREAMING)

00:09:22.813 --> 00:09:23.814
Could be a trap.

00:09:25.983 --> 00:09:27.318
Shield-wall!

00:09:54.886 --> 00:09:56.180
Open.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:14.614
Where have

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:14.614
they all gone?

00:10:15.824 --> 00:10:17.451
There should

00:10:15.824 --> 00:10:17.451
be treasure.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.580
He said there

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.580
would be treasure.

00:10:22.914 --> 00:10:24.708
Why do you always

00:10:22.914 --> 00:10:24.708
listen to him?

00:10:28.045 --> 00:10:29.338
Where is it?

00:10:31.382 --> 00:10:32.632
It's over there.

00:10:40.391 --> 00:10:42.642
This? This is

00:10:40.391 --> 00:10:42.642
not treasure.

00:10:42.684 --> 00:10:44.728
This is an empty

00:10:42.684 --> 00:10:44.728
wooden table.

00:10:49.107 --> 00:10:51.235
You are mistaken,

00:10:49.107 --> 00:10:51.235
King Horik.

00:10:51.276 --> 00:10:53.487
The treasure is here.

00:10:53.529 --> 00:10:55.197
You're standing on it.

00:10:53.529 --> 00:10:55.197
(KNOCKS)

00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:02.120
(STRAINING)

00:11:03.705 --> 00:11:05.374
(GRUNTING)

00:11:07.501 --> 00:11:08.627
(LAUGHS)

00:11:08.668 --> 00:11:10.087
You were right!

00:11:10.128 --> 00:11:12.256
(MEN LAUGHING)

00:11:12.297 --> 00:11:13.673
Look, it's treasure!

00:11:16.635 --> 00:11:18.095
How did you know?

00:11:18.845 --> 00:11:20.138
It is a Christian habit,

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:23.517
to bury the bones,

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:23.517
of the revered dead,

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:23.517
beneath the altar.

00:11:23.559 --> 00:11:24.684
Ragnar!

00:11:29.356 --> 00:11:31.024
HORIK: Let me see that.

00:11:31.066 --> 00:11:33.569
(TREASURE CLATTERING)

00:11:33.611 --> 00:11:35.613
(MEN LAUGHING)

00:11:36.614 --> 00:11:38.407
Who was this?

00:11:38.449 --> 00:11:41.452
It must be

00:11:38.449 --> 00:11:41.452
Saint Birinus.

00:11:41.493 --> 00:11:45.705
You keep talking to me

00:11:41.493 --> 00:11:45.705
like I know what

00:11:41.493 --> 00:11:45.705
a saint is.

00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:49.334
A saint is a man

00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:49.334
who has lived a

00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:49.334
particularly holy life,

00:11:49.376 --> 00:11:51.545
performed some miracle,

00:11:51.587 --> 00:11:54.798
or been martyred,

00:11:51.587 --> 00:11:54.798
killed, for their beliefs.

00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:56.634
MAN: It's all gold!

00:11:56.675 --> 00:11:59.344
But I am dead.

00:11:56.675 --> 00:11:59.344
What use can I be?

00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:03.014
(CHUCKLES)

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:06.017
Christians

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:06.017
believe that the bones,

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:06.017
can still exert benediction.

00:12:07.018 --> 00:12:08.562
Can perform miracles.

00:12:12.023 --> 00:12:14.610
What is a miracle?

00:12:14.652 --> 00:12:19.072
Miracles are things

00:12:14.652 --> 00:12:19.072
which are impossible to do.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.118
HORIK: Take it all.

00:12:24.703 --> 00:12:25.996
It's heavy.

00:12:35.046 --> 00:12:36.006
Wait.

00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:50.812
MAN: What do they want?

00:12:50.854 --> 00:12:51.771
(WOMAN GASPS)

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:53.691
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.885
(SHUDDERING)

00:13:36.316 --> 00:13:37.442
No! Stop!

00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:38.943
(GROANS)

00:13:41.196 --> 00:13:42.822
(GASPING)

00:14:01.466 --> 00:14:03.468
(SPEAKING

00:14:01.466 --> 00:14:03.468
IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:14:07.264 --> 00:14:08.473
(ATHELSTAN SPEAKING

00:14:07.264 --> 00:14:08.473
IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:14:08.515 --> 00:14:09.641
Hide!

00:14:09.683 --> 00:14:12.936
You speak

00:14:09.683 --> 00:14:12.936
our language. How?

00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:15.897
It doesn't matter.

00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:15.897
Just do as I say. Hide.

00:14:15.939 --> 00:14:18.567
Hide, or they

00:14:15.939 --> 00:14:18.567
will kill you.

00:14:15.939 --> 00:14:18.567
You're one of us.

00:14:20.819 --> 00:14:23.113
Once.

00:14:20.819 --> 00:14:23.113
Then, I will

00:14:20.819 --> 00:14:23.113
tell you this.

00:14:24.197 --> 00:14:26.157
One day,

00:14:24.197 --> 00:14:26.157
you will be caught.

00:14:26.199 --> 00:14:28.577
We will catch you

00:14:26.199 --> 00:14:28.577
and crucify you,

00:14:28.619 --> 00:14:31.162
for an apostate is the

00:14:28.619 --> 00:14:31.162
lowest, and the vilest,

00:14:28.619 --> 00:14:31.162
of all creatures,

00:14:31.204 --> 00:14:32.706
in the eyes of God.

00:14:34.625 --> 00:14:35.875
Oh.

00:14:56.313 --> 00:14:57.439
(IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:14:57.481 --> 00:14:59.357
He's coming with us.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.414
(SCREAMING)

00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:21.463
(IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:15:21.505 --> 00:15:23.965
Here is their main priest.

00:15:25.676 --> 00:15:28.261
You preach against our gods.

00:15:32.474 --> 00:15:37.020
You say there is only one God,

00:15:32.474 --> 00:15:37.020
but you are a liar

00:15:32.474 --> 00:15:37.020
and an old fool.

00:15:38.605 --> 00:15:42.860
The gods hate you,

00:15:38.605 --> 00:15:42.860
but I hate you even more.

00:15:44.986 --> 00:15:46.864
(SPEAKING LATIN)

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:48.990
(GROANS)

00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:50.950
(MEN LAUGHING)

00:15:53.495 --> 00:15:54.746
(IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:15:54.788 --> 00:15:59.209
Tie him up.

00:15:54.788 --> 00:15:59.209
Let us have some fun with him.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.418
(CHEERING)

00:16:12.389 --> 00:16:14.265
What will

00:16:12.389 --> 00:16:14.265
happen to him?

00:16:14.307 --> 00:16:16.476
You just wait

00:16:14.307 --> 00:16:16.476
and see, Priest.

00:16:19.187 --> 00:16:21.064
(MEN LAUGH)

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.028
(PRIEST PRAYING IN LATIN)

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.988
(GROANS)

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.988
(MEN CHEER)

00:16:30.657 --> 00:16:34.077
(CONTINUES PRAYING)

00:16:36.914 --> 00:16:40.124
(RUSTLING)

00:16:36.914 --> 00:16:40.124
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

00:16:59.394 --> 00:17:01.020
(MAN CHEERS)

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.837
MAN: More treasure!

00:17:25.879 --> 00:17:27.046
Here!

00:17:53.615 --> 00:17:55.241
(GROANS)

00:17:53.615 --> 00:17:55.241
(MEN CHEERING)

00:17:59.537 --> 00:18:01.080
(LAUGHING)

00:18:03.834 --> 00:18:07.170
(PRIEST PRAYING IN LATIN)

00:18:11.466 --> 00:18:13.010
(MEN CHEER)

00:18:14.177 --> 00:18:16.429
(CONTINUES PRAYING)

00:18:17.597 --> 00:18:19.098
FLOKI: Is he still talking?

00:18:20.017 --> 00:18:21.726
Tough old goat.

00:18:21.768 --> 00:18:24.688
HORIK: Erlendur, quiet him.

00:18:21.768 --> 00:18:24.688
Right in his mouth.

00:18:24.729 --> 00:18:26.606
(GASPING)

00:18:30.944 --> 00:18:33.697
(PRIEST CONTINUES PRAYING)

00:18:50.421 --> 00:18:52.049
(GASPS)

00:18:54.009 --> 00:18:56.344
(BLESSING IN LATIN)

00:18:57.888 --> 00:19:01.892
Suffer no more,

00:18:57.888 --> 00:19:01.892
but trust in

00:18:57.888 --> 00:19:01.892
thy salvation.

00:19:01.933 --> 00:19:03.810
(GROANS WEAKLY)

00:19:01.933 --> 00:19:03.810
(SLICES)

00:19:25.248 --> 00:19:28.167
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

00:19:41.431 --> 00:19:44.517
Mother,

00:19:41.431 --> 00:19:44.517
why would you allow him

00:19:41.431 --> 00:19:44.517
to do that to you?

00:19:44.559 --> 00:19:45.977
What are you

00:19:44.559 --> 00:19:45.977
talking about?

00:19:46.019 --> 00:19:47.562
Your husband,

00:19:46.019 --> 00:19:47.562
Earl Sigvard.

00:19:47.604 --> 00:19:48.521
I saw him.

00:19:49.981 --> 00:19:51.274
Bjorn, please.

00:19:51.315 --> 00:19:52.275
Please what?

00:19:54.111 --> 00:19:55.737
Has he

00:19:54.111 --> 00:19:55.737
hit you before?

00:19:57.572 --> 00:19:58.865
Will you let

00:19:57.572 --> 00:19:58.865
him hit you again?

00:19:58.907 --> 00:20:00.742
It will never

00:19:58.907 --> 00:20:00.742
happen again.

00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:04.037
If it does,

00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:04.037
I'll kill him.

00:20:04.788 --> 00:20:06.123
I said it won't.

00:20:09.584 --> 00:20:11.544
What would

00:20:09.584 --> 00:20:11.544
Ragnar say?

00:20:14.297 --> 00:20:15.799
What has it to do

00:20:14.297 --> 00:20:15.799
with your father?

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.008
Nothing.

00:20:18.927 --> 00:20:21.096
Sometimes I think

00:20:18.927 --> 00:20:21.096
of him.

00:20:21.138 --> 00:20:23.181
I miss him.

00:20:21.138 --> 00:20:23.181
I can't help it.

00:20:25.016 --> 00:20:27.435
Of course not.

00:20:25.016 --> 00:20:27.435
You're his son.

00:20:29.062 --> 00:20:31.314
You must

00:20:29.062 --> 00:20:31.314
always be proud.

00:20:31.355 --> 00:20:33.650
As should you,

00:20:31.355 --> 00:20:33.650
for being his wife.

00:20:48.832 --> 00:20:50.875
(CHILDREN PLAYING)

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.183
(SIGHS)

00:21:19.029 --> 00:21:20.279
Another son?

00:21:19.029 --> 00:21:20.279
(BABY COOS)

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:21.906
Yes.

00:21:23.825 --> 00:21:25.118
What is his name?

00:21:26.203 --> 00:21:28.287
Sigurd,

00:21:26.203 --> 00:21:28.287
after my father.

00:21:43.053 --> 00:21:44.888
Sigurd Snake-in-the-Eye.

00:21:52.478 --> 00:21:55.065
MAN: Close the gate!

00:21:55.106 --> 00:21:58.693
EDMUND:

00:21:55.106 --> 00:21:58.693
Your Majesty, you have heard

00:21:55.106 --> 00:21:58.693
of the attack on Winchester?

00:22:00.653 --> 00:22:01.863
Of course.

00:22:03.489 --> 00:22:04.908
I grieve.

00:22:04.949 --> 00:22:08.327
EDMUND: The martyrdom of

00:22:04.949 --> 00:22:08.327
my fellow bishop,

00:22:04.949 --> 00:22:08.327
Bishop Swithern.

00:22:09.453 --> 00:22:11.581
A fine Christian.

00:22:11.622 --> 00:22:13.083
ECBERT: Praise be to God.

00:22:14.876 --> 00:22:17.754
There are those who ask,

00:22:14.876 --> 00:22:17.754
why we did not do more,

00:22:17.795 --> 00:22:22.341
to protect our

00:22:17.795 --> 00:22:22.341
brothers and sisters,

00:22:17.795 --> 00:22:22.341
at such an important site.

00:22:23.676 --> 00:22:25.887
ECBERT: Are there?

00:22:25.929 --> 00:22:28.765
What answer did you give them,

00:22:25.929 --> 00:22:28.765
My Lord Eadric?

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:35.313
Perhaps he did not

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:35.313
have an answer.

00:22:35.354 --> 00:22:38.733
I've never found Lord Eadric

00:22:35.354 --> 00:22:38.733
to be at a loss for words.

00:22:38.775 --> 00:22:40.818
(MEN LAUGH)

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:44.197
I confess, that

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:44.197
in this case, it's true.

00:22:44.989 --> 00:22:46.783
I had no ready answer.

00:22:46.824 --> 00:22:51.788
No, because it's always easier

00:22:46.824 --> 00:22:51.788
to be wise, after the fact,

00:22:46.824 --> 00:22:51.788
is it not?

00:22:55.292 --> 00:22:57.127
My kingdom is very large.

00:22:57.168 --> 00:22:59.254
There are many

00:22:57.168 --> 00:22:59.254
important sites.

00:23:00.213 --> 00:23:03.841
Could I protect

00:23:00.213 --> 00:23:03.841
all of them? No.

00:23:03.883 --> 00:23:07.304
Did I want to discover

00:23:03.883 --> 00:23:07.304
where the pagans

00:23:03.883 --> 00:23:07.304
would strike?

00:23:07.845 --> 00:23:09.055
Yes.

00:23:10.348 --> 00:23:12.600
For now I know

00:23:10.348 --> 00:23:12.600
where they are.

00:23:12.642 --> 00:23:17.272
So Bishop Swithern

00:23:12.642 --> 00:23:17.272
was a necessary

00:23:12.642 --> 00:23:17.272
sacrifice.

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:23.153
As a man of God,

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:23.153
I assumed he welcomed

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:23.153
the opportunity for martyrdom.

00:23:25.863 --> 00:23:29.075
Or do you disagree?

00:23:25.863 --> 00:23:29.075
Oh, no, Sire.

00:23:29.117 --> 00:23:32.954
All of the cloth,

00:23:29.117 --> 00:23:32.954
would welcome martyrdom,

00:23:29.117 --> 00:23:32.954
in the cause of our faith,

00:23:32.996 --> 00:23:34.872
service of our

00:23:32.996 --> 00:23:34.872
lord Jesus Christ.

00:23:37.708 --> 00:23:39.961
Good.

00:23:40.003 --> 00:23:44.674
Because I'm going to

00:23:40.003 --> 00:23:44.674
offer you, precisely

00:23:40.003 --> 00:23:44.674
that same opportunity,

00:23:46.759 --> 00:23:48.136
My Lord Bishop.

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:54.225
And, I trust,

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:54.225
very soon.

00:24:07.947 --> 00:24:09.407
(SIGHS DEEPLY)

00:24:22.253 --> 00:24:25.215
TORSTEIN: It's times like this

00:24:22.253 --> 00:24:25.215
I miss our friend Arne.

00:24:25.256 --> 00:24:27.508
He could always make us laugh.

00:24:27.550 --> 00:24:29.927
Even in the darkest moments.

00:24:29.969 --> 00:24:33.556
Now, he's making

00:24:29.969 --> 00:24:33.556
the gods laugh.

00:24:33.597 --> 00:24:37.476
That's why they

00:24:33.597 --> 00:24:37.476
took him from us,

00:24:33.597 --> 00:24:37.476
'cause they were jealous.

00:24:40.604 --> 00:24:41.939
(CHUCKLES)

00:24:41.981 --> 00:24:42.732
Speaking of gods...

00:24:49.488 --> 00:24:51.490
I have something

00:24:49.488 --> 00:24:51.490
for you, Athelstan.

00:24:59.040 --> 00:25:00.375
Don't you want it?

00:25:01.834 --> 00:25:04.503
Are these not

00:25:01.834 --> 00:25:04.503
the images of your god?

00:25:06.089 --> 00:25:09.550
I told you before,

00:25:06.089 --> 00:25:09.550
and I will tell you again.

00:25:09.592 --> 00:25:11.844
My god is Odin,

00:25:09.592 --> 00:25:11.844
the Allfather.

00:25:11.886 --> 00:25:13.512
I know you've told me.

00:25:14.513 --> 00:25:17.225
Only, I don't believe you.

00:25:19.560 --> 00:25:21.062
And this?

00:25:21.104 --> 00:25:23.314
Ragnar gave me this.

00:25:23.356 --> 00:25:25.858
Wearing a dog turd

00:25:23.356 --> 00:25:25.858
doesn't make you a dog.

00:25:27.818 --> 00:25:28.861
Oh!

00:25:32.990 --> 00:25:35.118
I have something

00:25:32.990 --> 00:25:35.118
else for you.

00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:42.959
The hand of your

00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:42.959
holy man, I believe.

00:25:45.002 --> 00:25:46.337
(CHUCKLES)

00:25:47.755 --> 00:25:51.842
So tell me,

00:25:47.755 --> 00:25:51.842
how do you

00:25:47.755 --> 00:25:51.842
find England?

00:25:54.887 --> 00:25:56.473
It is a pleasant land,

00:25:57.390 --> 00:25:59.558
rich with treasure.

00:25:59.600 --> 00:26:02.520
You are right.

00:25:59.600 --> 00:26:02.520
This land is rich.

00:26:04.688 --> 00:26:08.192
But here,

00:26:04.688 --> 00:26:08.192
here is the

00:26:04.688 --> 00:26:08.192
real treasure.

00:26:08.234 --> 00:26:09.527
(SMELLS)

00:26:11.279 --> 00:26:12.947
Earth?

00:26:12.989 --> 00:26:16.117
Have you not seen?

00:26:12.989 --> 00:26:16.117
Everywhere we go,

00:26:12.989 --> 00:26:16.117
there are crops.

00:26:16.159 --> 00:26:18.411
There is food growing.

00:26:18.453 --> 00:26:21.498
I am a farmer and

00:26:18.453 --> 00:26:21.498
the son of a farmer,

00:26:21.539 --> 00:26:24.750
and this is what

00:26:21.539 --> 00:26:24.750
I understand.

00:26:24.792 --> 00:26:28.087
Compared to

00:26:24.792 --> 00:26:28.087
our poor countries

00:26:24.792 --> 00:26:28.087
where it is hard to farm,

00:26:28.129 --> 00:26:29.588
hard to live,

00:26:30.173 --> 00:26:32.425
here, it is easy.

00:26:34.677 --> 00:26:38.639
If we lived here,

00:26:34.677 --> 00:26:38.639
we could feed everybody.

00:26:34.677 --> 00:26:38.639
There would be no hunger.

00:26:39.974 --> 00:26:43.644
I like your thinking,

00:26:39.974 --> 00:26:43.644
but here is my question.

00:26:43.686 --> 00:26:46.397
Will the Saxons

00:26:43.686 --> 00:26:46.397
simply invite us

00:26:43.686 --> 00:26:46.397
to live among them?

00:26:46.439 --> 00:26:47.524
Hmm?

00:26:50.734 --> 00:26:54.822
(PEOPLE CHEERING LOUDLY)

00:26:54.864 --> 00:26:57.283
(APPLAUDING)

00:26:58.535 --> 00:27:00.744
(CHEERING)

00:27:01.662 --> 00:27:05.458
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

00:27:29.566 --> 00:27:33.444
Friends, family,

00:27:29.566 --> 00:27:33.444
what's left of it,

00:27:35.446 --> 00:27:39.116
so, I am married

00:27:35.446 --> 00:27:39.116
for the second time.

00:27:39.158 --> 00:27:42.078
As most of you know,

00:27:39.158 --> 00:27:42.078
my first marriage

00:27:39.158 --> 00:27:42.078
lasted less than an hour,

00:27:42.119 --> 00:27:45.122
because my own brother

00:27:42.119 --> 00:27:45.122
poisoned the drinks that day.

00:27:47.041 --> 00:27:48.709
Of course, the same thing

00:27:47.041 --> 00:27:48.709
can never happen twice,

00:27:48.751 --> 00:27:50.294
so let the wine

00:27:48.751 --> 00:27:50.294
be poured.

00:27:50.336 --> 00:27:52.296
(CHEERING)

00:27:52.338 --> 00:27:54.424
(BANGING TABLE)

00:28:03.558 --> 00:28:06.603
Now, who will be the first

00:28:03.558 --> 00:28:06.603
to drink in celebration?

00:28:12.900 --> 00:28:13.943
I will.

00:28:22.243 --> 00:28:24.954
No. No,

00:28:22.243 --> 00:28:24.954
I could not bear it.

00:28:22.243 --> 00:28:24.954
Not a second time.

00:28:24.995 --> 00:28:26.705
Let me taste the wine.

00:28:34.547 --> 00:28:35.590
(COUGHING)

00:28:44.056 --> 00:28:45.433
That's good enough.

00:28:45.475 --> 00:28:46.725
(CHEERING)

00:29:05.786 --> 00:29:08.456
I have something

00:29:05.786 --> 00:29:08.456
else important to say.

00:29:08.498 --> 00:29:10.082
I don't wish to

00:29:08.498 --> 00:29:10.082
dampen the celebrations,

00:29:10.124 --> 00:29:13.127
but you all know

00:29:10.124 --> 00:29:13.127
that the agreement

00:29:10.124 --> 00:29:13.127
between myself,

00:29:13.169 --> 00:29:16.964
King Horik and

00:29:13.169 --> 00:29:16.964
Ragnar Lothbrok

00:29:13.169 --> 00:29:16.964
has been broken.

00:29:17.006 --> 00:29:19.467
They have

00:29:17.006 --> 00:29:19.467
gone raiding west

00:29:17.006 --> 00:29:19.467
without me, without us,

00:29:19.509 --> 00:29:22.761
which is an insult

00:29:19.509 --> 00:29:22.761
not only to myself,

00:29:19.509 --> 00:29:22.761
but to all of you.

00:29:22.803 --> 00:29:26.432
And now, also to my wife

00:29:22.803 --> 00:29:26.432
and to my wife's family.

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:32.813
I have to do

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:32.813
something about

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:32.813
this insult.

00:29:32.855 --> 00:29:35.858
Frankly, I blame

00:29:32.855 --> 00:29:35.858
King Horik more

00:29:32.855 --> 00:29:35.858
for what has happened,

00:29:35.899 --> 00:29:39.903
but at the same time, consider

00:29:35.899 --> 00:29:39.903
what is happening to

00:29:35.899 --> 00:29:39.903
Earl Ragnar's lands.

00:29:40.904 --> 00:29:43.407
He has abandoned them,

00:29:43.449 --> 00:29:46.410
to the care of his wife,

00:29:43.449 --> 00:29:46.410
and his drunken brother.

00:29:47.203 --> 00:29:49.455
(LAUGHING)

00:29:49.497 --> 00:29:53.751
In order to punish those,

00:29:49.497 --> 00:29:53.751
who have insulted

00:29:49.497 --> 00:29:53.751
me and my family,

00:29:53.792 --> 00:29:57.380
I declare today, that

00:29:53.792 --> 00:29:57.380
I will seek vengeance,

00:29:53.792 --> 00:29:57.380
against Ragnar Lothbrok.

00:29:59.298 --> 00:30:05.763
By all our gods,

00:29:59.298 --> 00:30:05.763
I swear, that we will

00:29:59.298 --> 00:30:05.763
seize, all his lands,

00:30:05.804 --> 00:30:09.183
and that I will repay,

00:30:05.804 --> 00:30:09.183
his brother's

00:30:05.804 --> 00:30:09.183
treachery, with the ax.

00:30:09.225 --> 00:30:11.310
(CHEERING)

00:30:49.265 --> 00:30:51.850
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:30:49.265 --> 00:30:51.850
Who can speak to us?

00:30:56.146 --> 00:30:57.147
I can.

00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:04.447
I have been sent

00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:04.447
here by Ecbert,

00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:04.447
King of Wessex.

00:31:04.488 --> 00:31:09.868
The King regrets

00:31:04.488 --> 00:31:09.868
your attack, on the

00:31:04.488 --> 00:31:09.868
holy church at Winchester.

00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:14.791
He wonders how much

00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:14.791
longer, you intend to

00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:14.791
remain in his kingdom.

00:31:15.833 --> 00:31:16.875
(CLEARS THROAT)

00:31:18.711 --> 00:31:21.880
Well, that depends.

00:31:24.425 --> 00:31:26.051
EDMUND: Upon what?

00:31:27.428 --> 00:31:30.306
Upon what he'll

00:31:27.428 --> 00:31:30.306
offer us to leave.

00:31:32.015 --> 00:31:35.770
Or what he'll

00:31:32.015 --> 00:31:35.770
offer us to stay.

00:31:39.148 --> 00:31:41.150
Stay?

00:31:41.191 --> 00:31:45.529
Yes, we want to make

00:31:41.191 --> 00:31:45.529
peace with the King.

00:31:47.406 --> 00:31:48.866
Peace.

00:31:52.453 --> 00:31:54.622
(GROANS)

00:31:52.453 --> 00:31:54.622
(MEN LAUGH)

00:31:54.664 --> 00:31:56.915
So we don't have to

00:31:54.664 --> 00:31:56.915
kill any more of you.

00:31:58.167 --> 00:32:02.463
I will relay your

00:31:58.167 --> 00:32:02.463
message to the King.

00:32:04.423 --> 00:32:06.049
(FLOKI CHUCKLES)

00:32:07.926 --> 00:32:09.386
(SPEAKING IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:32:13.850 --> 00:32:14.851
(GROANS)

00:32:18.103 --> 00:32:19.396
(LAUGHS)

00:32:19.438 --> 00:32:21.357
(GRUNTING)

00:32:23.942 --> 00:32:25.695
(STRAINING)

00:32:28.739 --> 00:32:30.949
(MEN LAUGHING)

00:32:35.412 --> 00:32:36.497
(GROANS)

00:32:36.539 --> 00:32:38.081
(LAUGHING)

00:32:45.840 --> 00:32:47.633
(NEIGHS)

00:32:50.845 --> 00:32:52.971
SIGVARD: Not hungry, Bjorn?

00:32:53.890 --> 00:32:55.182
No.

00:32:55.224 --> 00:32:56.517
Any reason?

00:32:56.559 --> 00:32:57.976
No reason.

00:32:58.895 --> 00:33:00.270
Are you unhappy?

00:33:05.902 --> 00:33:08.070
What can I do to

00:33:05.902 --> 00:33:08.070
make you happy?

00:33:10.155 --> 00:33:12.115
Shall I

00:33:10.155 --> 00:33:12.115
raid one of my

00:33:10.155 --> 00:33:12.115
unsuspecting neighbors,

00:33:12.157 --> 00:33:15.077
so you can show off

00:33:12.157 --> 00:33:15.077
your fighting skills?

00:33:15.118 --> 00:33:17.747
And maybe slaughter

00:33:15.118 --> 00:33:17.747
them all?

00:33:17.788 --> 00:33:21.083
Show that you are

00:33:17.788 --> 00:33:21.083
truly the son of

00:33:17.788 --> 00:33:21.083
Ragnar Lothbrok?

00:33:21.124 --> 00:33:22.626
(MEN LAUGHING)

00:33:24.253 --> 00:33:26.004
SIGVARD:

00:33:24.253 --> 00:33:26.004
No, believe me,

00:33:26.046 --> 00:33:28.006
I do not like to

00:33:26.046 --> 00:33:28.006
see you so solemn.

00:33:29.675 --> 00:33:32.845
So tell me,

00:33:29.675 --> 00:33:32.845
what can I do?

00:33:36.098 --> 00:33:39.351
You can let me go

00:33:36.098 --> 00:33:39.351
live in a cabin

00:33:36.098 --> 00:33:39.351
in the mountains.

00:33:39.393 --> 00:33:42.020
By yourself?

00:33:39.393 --> 00:33:42.020
In the mountains?

00:33:39.393 --> 00:33:42.020
Yes.

00:33:43.021 --> 00:33:45.065
I'd like to test myself.

00:33:45.691 --> 00:33:47.944
Get away from all this.

00:33:47.985 --> 00:33:52.615
All these servants.

00:33:47.985 --> 00:33:52.615
All these people

00:33:47.985 --> 00:33:52.615
doing everything for us.

00:33:52.656 --> 00:33:55.785
I want to know what

00:33:52.656 --> 00:33:55.785
is essential to life.

00:33:55.826 --> 00:33:57.703
What is

00:33:55.826 --> 00:33:57.703
really important.

00:34:01.874 --> 00:34:03.250
Will you let me?

00:34:05.628 --> 00:34:07.713
No. Of course not.

00:34:08.965 --> 00:34:10.549
I am the earl here.

00:34:12.259 --> 00:34:15.763
What would folk

00:34:12.259 --> 00:34:15.763
think, if I let my

00:34:12.259 --> 00:34:15.763
beloved stepson starve

00:34:15.805 --> 00:34:18.515
or freeze to death,

00:34:15.805 --> 00:34:18.515
in some mountain pigsty?

00:34:19.475 --> 00:34:21.018
(MEN LAUGH)

00:34:21.059 --> 00:34:23.813
SIGVARD:

00:34:21.059 --> 00:34:23.813
You understand that,

00:34:21.059 --> 00:34:23.813
don't you, my boy?

00:34:23.854 --> 00:34:25.731
In any case,

00:34:25.773 --> 00:34:29.693
I have solemnly sworn

00:34:25.773 --> 00:34:29.693
to Lagertha, that I

00:34:25.773 --> 00:34:29.693
shall take care of you.

00:34:30.569 --> 00:34:31.988
And I will.

00:34:52.633 --> 00:34:53.843
Rollo!

00:34:56.386 --> 00:34:58.138
Rollo, wake up.

00:34:56.386 --> 00:34:58.138
What?

00:35:00.140 --> 00:35:02.184
What is it?

00:35:00.140 --> 00:35:02.184
There are boats.

00:35:07.690 --> 00:35:09.066
SIGGY: Who are they?

00:35:10.192 --> 00:35:12.235
ROLLO:

00:35:10.192 --> 00:35:12.235
I think I can guess.

00:35:12.277 --> 00:35:13.529
Go back to the town.

00:35:14.404 --> 00:35:16.032
Find anyone

00:35:14.404 --> 00:35:16.032
who can fight.

00:35:16.073 --> 00:35:17.992
Anyone who can

00:35:16.073 --> 00:35:17.992
hold a weapon.

00:35:19.493 --> 00:35:20.953
We're under attack.

00:35:32.255 --> 00:35:34.550
Rollo, what is it?

00:35:32.255 --> 00:35:34.550
What is happening?

00:35:34.591 --> 00:35:37.594
Jarl Borg.

00:35:34.591 --> 00:35:37.594
He has come

00:35:34.591 --> 00:35:37.594
back to attack us.

00:35:38.220 --> 00:35:39.722
Jarl Borg?

00:35:39.763 --> 00:35:41.057
I'm sure

00:35:39.763 --> 00:35:41.057
it is him.

00:35:42.599 --> 00:35:46.103
Ragnar and King Horik

00:35:42.599 --> 00:35:46.103
broke their

00:35:42.599 --> 00:35:46.103
agreement with him.

00:35:46.144 --> 00:35:48.438
He has returned to

00:35:46.144 --> 00:35:48.438
gain his revenge.

00:35:48.480 --> 00:35:50.190
What are we

00:35:48.480 --> 00:35:50.190
going to do?

00:35:52.317 --> 00:35:54.737
What do you think

00:35:52.317 --> 00:35:54.737
we're going to do?

00:35:54.778 --> 00:35:56.154
We're going to fight.

00:35:57.948 --> 00:36:00.743
Come. Go! Go!

00:36:00.784 --> 00:36:02.661
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

00:36:06.206 --> 00:36:08.709
ROLLO: Torfin! Olaf!

00:36:06.206 --> 00:36:08.709
One of you on each flank.

00:36:11.211 --> 00:36:12.254
Help with the barricades.

00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.553
Ragnar has taken

00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.553
all of the best

00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.553
fighting men.

00:36:21.513 --> 00:36:23.181
Look what we have left.

00:36:27.436 --> 00:36:28.520
What are you doing?

00:36:28.562 --> 00:36:30.230
What does it look like?

00:36:30.272 --> 00:36:32.775
Not you.

00:36:30.272 --> 00:36:32.775
You are not

00:36:30.272 --> 00:36:32.775
a shield-maiden.

00:36:32.816 --> 00:36:34.192
You're not...

00:36:32.816 --> 00:36:34.192
Lagertha.

00:36:36.486 --> 00:36:39.907
Siggy, I need

00:36:36.486 --> 00:36:39.907
you to go back

00:36:36.486 --> 00:36:39.907
to the Great Hall.

00:36:39.949 --> 00:36:41.283
Find Princess Aslaug

00:36:39.949 --> 00:36:41.283
and her children,

00:36:41.324 --> 00:36:42.743
and take them up

00:36:41.324 --> 00:36:42.743
into the mountains.

00:36:42.785 --> 00:36:44.244
And then what?

00:36:42.785 --> 00:36:44.244
Wait.

00:36:45.537 --> 00:36:46.663
For what?

00:36:49.750 --> 00:36:52.586
For whatever

00:36:49.750 --> 00:36:52.586
the gods have decided

00:36:49.750 --> 00:36:52.586
is about to happen.

00:36:53.921 --> 00:36:55.798
Now go.

00:36:55.839 --> 00:36:58.216
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

00:37:24.534 --> 00:37:25.869
Come on.

00:37:27.079 --> 00:37:29.331
This way.

00:37:27.079 --> 00:37:29.331
To the mountains.

00:37:29.372 --> 00:37:32.626
This way.

00:37:29.372 --> 00:37:32.626
Go, Hvitserk.

00:37:29.372 --> 00:37:32.626
Run. Quickly.

00:37:41.635 --> 00:37:43.345
Sail down!

00:37:43.386 --> 00:37:45.597
(HORN BLOWS)

00:37:49.059 --> 00:37:50.853
Row! Row!

00:37:58.610 --> 00:38:00.612
ROLLO: Stay strong!

00:38:00.654 --> 00:38:02.280
Don't make it

00:38:00.654 --> 00:38:02.280
easy for them!

00:38:03.532 --> 00:38:05.325
Light the fires!

00:38:27.764 --> 00:38:29.432
(MEN SHOUTING)

00:38:32.477 --> 00:38:33.395
(BANGING)

00:38:34.021 --> 00:38:35.689
ROLLO: Archers!

00:38:35.731 --> 00:38:38.316
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:46.324
Oars!

00:38:50.746 --> 00:38:51.997
ROLLO: Hold your places!

00:39:02.632 --> 00:39:03.759
Jump ship!

00:39:03.800 --> 00:39:05.343
(SHOUTS)

00:39:06.095 --> 00:39:07.554
Go!

00:39:07.596 --> 00:39:10.140
(SHOUTING)

00:39:13.102 --> 00:39:14.103
(GROANS)

00:39:18.732 --> 00:39:19.775
(GROANS)

00:39:32.079 --> 00:39:33.080
(GROANS)

00:39:35.082 --> 00:39:36.458
(GRUNTING)

00:39:36.499 --> 00:39:37.500
(SCREAMS)

00:39:42.672 --> 00:39:43.548
(GROANS)

00:39:44.591 --> 00:39:45.383
(GROANS)

00:39:46.593 --> 00:39:48.511
As fast as you can!

00:39:46.593 --> 00:39:48.511
Shields!

00:40:05.195 --> 00:40:06.404
BOY: Rollo!

00:40:24.673 --> 00:40:25.841
Fall back!

00:40:56.205 --> 00:40:57.455
(SHOUTS)

00:41:00.417 --> 00:41:02.169
Fall back!

00:41:02.211 --> 00:41:03.795
Back to the

00:41:02.211 --> 00:41:03.795
marketplace.

00:41:07.590 --> 00:41:08.633
Move!

00:41:11.469 --> 00:41:13.471
That's right,

00:41:11.469 --> 00:41:13.471
Rollo, run!

00:41:14.472 --> 00:41:16.225
Run, like

00:41:14.472 --> 00:41:16.225
you always do.

00:41:17.517 --> 00:41:19.144
(SHOUTING)

00:41:43.835 --> 00:41:44.836
(GRUNTS)

00:41:49.716 --> 00:41:50.592
Loose!

00:41:56.139 --> 00:41:57.433
Loose!

00:42:01.937 --> 00:42:03.188
Shield-wall!

00:42:20.414 --> 00:42:22.082
You can't win,

00:42:20.414 --> 00:42:22.082
Rollo!

00:42:24.084 --> 00:42:26.920
There is no disgrace,

00:42:24.084 --> 00:42:26.920
in the eyes of the gods,

00:42:24.084 --> 00:42:26.920
to save yourself

00:42:26.962 --> 00:42:28.546
for another day.

00:42:32.675 --> 00:42:33.551
(GROANS)

00:42:32.675 --> 00:42:33.551
(GASPING)

00:42:37.097 --> 00:42:41.059
Your first duty

00:42:37.097 --> 00:42:41.059
is to try and save

00:42:37.097 --> 00:42:41.059
the sons of Ragnar.

00:42:41.101 --> 00:42:42.727
Surrender!

00:42:45.230 --> 00:42:46.398
Rollo,

00:42:47.441 --> 00:42:48.942
let me speak for the gods,

00:42:48.984 --> 00:42:52.404
for I will shortly join them

00:42:48.984 --> 00:42:52.404
in their bright halls.

00:42:52.446 --> 00:42:56.032
But you, you have

00:42:52.446 --> 00:42:56.032
other work to do here.

00:42:57.867 --> 00:42:58.952
Go.

00:43:00.329 --> 00:43:02.789
I will tell the gods

00:43:00.329 --> 00:43:02.789
what you have done.

00:43:24.227 --> 00:43:26.229
Now do you surrender?

00:43:52.714 --> 00:43:53.882
(SHOUTS)

00:43:52.714 --> 00:43:53.882
(SCREAMS)

00:43:55.509 --> 00:43:58.053
(ALL SHOUTING)

00:45:02.909 --> 00:45:04.702
(LAUGHING)